# Test: the built le binary runs both inventory gates over the real
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#       checkout, reports the checkout-wide contract, and exposes the same
#       answers from every working directory and rendering.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-is-a-ze-binary AC-11 over the real tree and real registry,
#            and AC-7 for both ported tools against the artifact a developer
#            runs.
# PREVENTS: an implementation that passes isolated fixtures while disagreeing
#           with the checkout. The inventory walks the full tree and reads the
#           live plugin registry, so the fixture retains the substantial page,
#           plugin, command-shape, row-operator, ordering, and refusal checks.
#
# The product is compiled with the full feature set derived from
# feature-gates.txt. Its output artifact is written in the fixture directory;
# the checkout is only read.
#
# The timeout is declared because linking the full product precedes repeated
# full walks of the checkout.

option=timeout:value=900s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/le-inventory-answers
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
